## Python Instruction
Write a function to check if two strings are one edit away. An edit can be an insert, delete, or replace of a character.

## Python Solution
```python
def one_edit_away(first: str, second: str) -> bool:
    if len(first) > len(second):
        first, second = second, first
    if len(second) - len(first) > 1:
        return False
    for j, c in enumerate(first):
        if c != second[j]:
            if len(first) == len(second):
                return first[j+1:] == second[j+1:]
            else:
                return second[j+1:] == first[j:]
    return True
```

## Python Tests
assert one_edit_away("pale", "ple") == True
assert one_edit_away("pales", "pale") == True
assert one_edit_away("pale", "bale") == True
assert one_edit_away("pale", "bake") == False

## Canonical Elixir names (use verbatim)
- Module: `Solution`
- Function: `one_edit_away`

