Write a function `one_edit_away` that takes two strings and returns a boolean indicating whether they are exactly one edit apart. An edit is defined as inserting, deleting, or replacing a single character. If the strings are identical (zero edits), return false. If the difference in length is more than one, return false. The function should run in linear time relative to the length of the shorter string. Handle all edge cases, including empty strings.

